  "notes": {
    "why": "character runs round 7 (TFT, 11-17; the user: 「继续处理云顶的英雄吧」): his drawn run (Codex's spider legs, PR #711) moves only the legs - the neck, head, crest and the two small heads are one drawing that bobs a row on frames 1 and 5, so at game size he glided",
    "motion": "TFT's Baron has no run (his move is the burrow, Baron_GroundLoop) and no legs; the closest League build with his legs is Elise's spider form: EliseSpider_Run1 (1.067 s = two gait cycles) bobs her body 12 units on a 50-unit leg root, two beats a cycle, ~5.7 rows at his 23-row legs. His own idle (BaronNashor_Idle1) sinks and lifts his neck and head over the base (Neck / Spine_3 +-2.4 rows against the root) - the neck bobbing over a still base is his own motion",
    "body": "lock own: every frame keeps its own drawing (the small heads' mouths and the crest as drawn); its upper body - everything above row -17 (frame 1) and the neck column (the S curve and the teal belly with their outline, the claw arms' and the collar's violet squares left out) - lowered `shift` rows over the base (the abdomen, its violet collar, both claws and all eight legs, square for square as drawn): 0 5 3 0 0 5 3 0 on the drawn 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0, so the head is 6 rows (2.9 game px) lowest on frames 1 and 5 (all legs down: the landing of each tripod), half way up the frame after, high on the swing frames",
    "under": "own_under (rows from -6, frame 1, down, cols -9..18): the lowered neck slides behind its collar - only its own squares there take the lowered drawing, the collar's violet rims and the tip's outline stay in front (laid over, the rims went black and left 3x3 black blots)",
    "masks": "C:/t/par_work/run_tft7/_c7_work/bmask2.py: the neck's rows are frame 1's, each frame's own offset (the lower neck is drawn a row higher in frames 4, 6, 7: bneckoff.py)",
    "one": "the 1x run stays the installed drawings (keep_one: baronnashor_run_one); the lo_ run is made from the dense frames (installed lo_ outline was made before the dense frames were thinned: 130-155 outline squares a frame thinner, no shape change)",
    "variants": "base: lowest 6 rows (League's 5.7); b5: 5; b4: 4"
